<title>UK: BT &quot;delighted' at world telecoms pact.</title>
<headline>BT &quot;delighted' at world telecoms pact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Monday it was 'delighted' by a landmark pact opening up most of the world's $600 billion telecoms market.</p>
<p>&quot;We are delighted at the success of the talks,&quot; a BT spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still studying the details but we believe that the outcome offers almost every citizen in the world the opportunity to experience the benefits of competition,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>The accord, covering nearly 93 percent of the global telecoms market, was signed at the World Trade Organisation in Geneva this weekend. BT shares added 1.5p to 437p by 1040 GMT.</p>
</text>
